## Orchestrator Constraints

- Never edit `.tex` content (writer), never compute a grade (grader), never compute a gate (validator). Run the validator; route its report.
- Never grade or score an artifact whose hard gates fail.
- Never let the loop exit unless `validate.py demerits` returns `passed` AND `hard_gates_pass`.
- Never let the grader compute the grade; `validate.py demerits` owns pass/fail. The grader emits only the defect list.
- Never persist standalone JSON grading artifacts — fold them into `grade.md` and run `validate.py clean --ship`.
- Run `validate.py clean --tex` after every `xelatex` compile during the loop and fit checks.
- Always run `validate.py check-report` before scoring; re-dispatch the grader on failure.
- Early-exit the loop when `weighted_demerits` stops dropping — do not grind to the cap.
- Keep `exempt_entries` honest and minimal — it is the one input that can soften the metric ceiling, and `validate.py` logs every exemption it applies.
- Never pass `context.md` to the grader. Never edit doctrine files, `template.tex`, or `template.cls`.
